<title>BRAZIL: Brazil CMN approves Minas Gerais bank selloffs.</title>
<headline>Brazil CMN approves Minas Gerais bank selloffs.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council (CMN) has approved a plan by Minas Gerais state to privatize two banks and liquidate another, Central Bank president Gustavo Loyola said.</p>
<p>Minas Gerais, which had previously announced its intention to sell banks Credireal and Banco do Estado de Minas Gerais and liquidate mortgage bank Minas Caixa, would remain with only a development bank, Loyola said.</p>
</text>
